WEBVTT

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.600
Hey, are you all right?

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.700
This is my <i>third</i> report!

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.340
Do we really have to 
do these write-ups?

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.540
It'd be quicker just to explain orally.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.410
I see where you're coming from.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.920
But having a written record is important.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.210
Hang in there, Kukuru-san.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.290
The assistant director's giving you so much
work only because he has high hopes for you.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.630
Akari-chan, do you really believe that?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:39.970
You're so soft.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.020
Plankton.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.080
Yes, sir!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.040
Come up with some ideas 
for the project presentation ASAP.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.480
Project presentation?

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.150
We're using the first floor west wing.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.550
Think of a buzzworthy event 
that'll attract a lot of guests.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.700
Do it by tomorrow.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.350
Tomorrow?

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.320
Don't you think that's a bit—

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.540
That's all from me.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.950
Fine, sir!

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.630
I see. You need ideas by tomorrow, huh?

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.490
Yeah!

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:39.820
Can you believe it?

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.660
He just keeps pushing more work on me.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.620
He's such a slave driver.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.810
Sounds rough.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.740
But it also sounds good.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.370
It's an opportunity to get people 
to learn about sea life, right?

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.340
It'll be really rewarding, 
getting to choose what we're exhibiting.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.260
Yeah.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.530
We didn't have enough people 
or funding to do much at Gama Gama.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.660
But you might be able 
to do something new at Tingarla.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.600
You're right.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.100
Thanks, Fuuka.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.880
All right!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:23.160
I thought there were some preparations
underway for a big exhibit in the summer.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.870
That got postponed.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.640
But we can't just sit 
on our hands till then,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.470
so now we're scrambling 
to come up with a new plan.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.640
So that's why Kukuru-san's been tapped.

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.980
Welcome to the fish area.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.490
The spines on the porcupinefish 
are normally facing flat,

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.520
but they point up when its body inflates.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.830
Now, what do you think 
these spines are for?

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.760
Yeah, sounds good.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.140
Thank you.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.600
Kai-kun, you're up.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.780
Uh, all right.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.980
This is the porcupinefish.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.930
It's a kind of pufferfish.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.970
Do you have any questions or anything?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.930
Sorry.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.680
We'll have you do the next tour, Eiji-kun.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.420
Okay.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.380
Kai-kun, have something ready 
to talk about.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.480
It can be something 
you're more familiar with.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.610
Okay.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.410
Hello.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.490
Do you know where Chief Garandou is?

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.140
Dunno.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.380
I'm sure he's somewhere.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:36.480
The assistant director asked me 
to deliver some mail.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.160
No clue where the chief might be?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.040
Nope.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.840
He wasn't in the attendant room, either.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.010
I seriously can't find him.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.890
I saw the chief in the break room.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.170
Really?

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:50.990
Yeah.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.380
Thank you.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.680
Thanks, you saved me.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.820
You can deal with her from now on.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:04.000
Kuuya-kun, could you help Umi-yan-san 
when you're done here?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.600
A'ight.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.640
Don't "a'ight" me.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.070
We're at work.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.340
A'ight.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.500
I said...

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:35.770
Explain.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.050
Right!

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.920
The first one is an exhibit 
of dangerous sea animals.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.550
I thought it'd be fun to show off some
animals that you don't get to see often.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:46.450
<b><i>Diadema setosum</i></b>

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:46.450
<b>Red piranha</b>

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.450
Like piranhas, or other things 
that are particularly vicious.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.000
The next one is a killifish exhibit.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.460
Killifish are easy to keep, 
and they're popular right now.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.780
That one's a salamander.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.870
The one below that is deep sea fish.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:00.130
There's all sorts of unique critters. 
They're great!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:04.340
I want to talk about the plastic waste
problem and the endangerment of coral.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.550
Which of these can we do 
in two weeks?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:07.350
Eh?

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.110
I think we can do sea slugs.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.040
We won't have to borrow any 
from other aquariums,

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.200
since we can find them 
in nearby waters.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.010
Sea slugs, huh?

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.330
They aren't called jewels 
of the sea for nothing.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
<b><i>Phyllidia coelestis</i></b>

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
<b>Colorful 
Sea Slugs</b>

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
<b><i>Dermatobranchus ornatus</i></b>

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
<b><i>Ardaedoris cruenta</i></b>

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
<b><i>Tambja sagamiana</i></b>

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
<b><i>Goniobranchus coi</i></b>

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.480
They're really colorful, 
and you never get bored of them.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.330
But you don't really get a chance 
to get a good look at them at the shore.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:28.010
I'm absolutely certain it'll generate buzz 
if we show off lots of different kinds!

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.730
We'll do sea slugs, 
if you're that confident in them.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.660
Thank you!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.790
But we'll need to make some adjustments.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.600
Yes, sir!

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.410
We need more than five.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.630
We need at least eight.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.360
Sea slugs are hard to keep, though.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:44.700
It might put a lot of strain 
on the attendant team.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:45.920
Which team are you on?

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.680
The marketing team.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.430
That's right.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:53.850
You need to put the guests' feelings 
ahead of the attendant team's problems.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.930
That's how you gain customers 
and make profit.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.420
It's how we create a future for Tingarla.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.450
We don't have time.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:02.670
Hurry up and get it started.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:03.540
Yes, sir!

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.430
Wow.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:10.080
Her proposal got accepted.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.330
Sea slugs sound fun.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:15.290
Are sea slugs slugs in the sea?

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:16.250
Haven't you seen them?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.830
They're in the shallows.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.850
They're like slugs.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:22.880
Are you sure they're cute?

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.730
This space is pretty big.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.760
He's right. Five species might not be enough.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:32.660
Umi-yan.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.090
Kukuru-chan.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.010
Can I ask you about sea slugs?

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:38.940
Hi, long time.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.870
It's Misakino. Thank you for
your help at Gama Gama.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.270
There's something I'd like to ask you.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.060
There, done!

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.200
Now...

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:55.750
Kai!

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.040
Kai, do you have a minute?

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.220
Hurry!

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.420
Morning?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.410
Yeah.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.280
You have some time, 
since you're on the late shift, right?

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.140
Could you come 
to the shore with me?

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:13.380
Please?

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.140
Sure, I guess.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.240
Yay!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.610
See you tomorrow!

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.030
Based on my observations, 
your courtship behavior is shy,

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.060
modest, and difficult to read.

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.510
Courtship?

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:33.200
Did you know? The male prickleback fish 
builds a nest and dances in front of it.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:40.950
The male seahorse shows off its brood pouch 
to the female to request egg deposits.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.920
I think you'd be better off 
being just as obvious.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:45.900
What?

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:49.000
So she was the motivation behind
you becoming an aquarium attendant,

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.320
despite your parents being fishermen.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:54.380
I'll be rooting for your
successful courtship, in secret.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.020
Hey, I never...

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.650
It feels great, Kai!

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:07.800
Yeah.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.610
It feels great, Fuuka!

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:16.680
<i>Miyazawa-san's here, too.</i>

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.400
Heave ho.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.980
There's some. Look.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.830
Wow!

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:30.540
Umi-yan told me 
there are a lot of sea slugs here.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.590
I found some here, too.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.650
There are so many!

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:38.300
Verconia simplex and 
Hypselodoris purpureomaculosa.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:42.220
I know which sea sponges these kids eat, 
so we'll take them home.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:46.310
We don't know what <i>Tambja
sagamiana</i> eats, so it might not work.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:47.520
Huh?

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:48.690
What do you mean?

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:53.150
Sea slugs are super picky eaters.
They eat only certain things.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.190
So it's really important 
what we feed them.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:00.450
Some kinds of sea slugs eat sea sponges. 
Others eat sea moss or sea squirts.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:04.330
And they eat only fresh
natural stuff, so it's a pain.

00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:05.640
Seriously?

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:06.970
That's a pain.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:10.490
So I called an aquarium I'm acquainted with

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.460
and gathered information on what they eat.

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:17.580
In other words, there's
a lot that we don't know yet?

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.400
Yup!

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:19.840
This is going to be tough.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.970
There's so much to know about sea slugs!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.780
Let's check out the rocks over there.

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:30.770
They'll die out easily if we
gather too many from one spot.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:31.720
Okay.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.270
R-Right.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.280
Eat up lots.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:44.790
Chief Garandou.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.210
Yeah? What's up?

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:50.280
We're doing a sea-slug exhibit soon.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.790
May we have your cooperation?

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.900
This is the project proposal.

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.320
You sure do come up 
with challenging events.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:00.190
I guess I can't say "no" 
to the assistant director.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.820
When are we starting?

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:03.050
The end of next week.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.480
That's too soon.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.200
We had this problem 
with the behind-the-scenes tour.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.900
Couldn't you tell us earlier?

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.350
We need to prepare, too.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:10.850
Sorry.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.080
So what's the exhibit?

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.870
Eight kinds?

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:16.860
That's a lot.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:18.890
Can we cut it down by half?

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.490
That'll be difficult.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.510
You were an attendant before, weren't you?

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:25.030
Don't you know how hard
it is to keep sea slugs?

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.350
I understand.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:28.090
I do, but...

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.250
But I think the guests come first.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.160
Are you saying the attendants don't matter?

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.130
There, there.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.130
What do you plan to do for food?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.310
We know the species and where they feed.

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:40.590
We just need to gather some.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:43.660
Sea sponges and moss are delicate.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:45.350
We'll have to harvest them frequently.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.870
And telling them apart is difficult.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:51.130
If we spend time on food, 
we won't be able to finish our other work.

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:53.350
How about giving up on food?

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.600
Keep them unfed, huh?

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:56.570
We can't do that!

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.780
It'd be cruel not to feed them!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.130
It's a short exhibit, though.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:02.380
I think we should consider it.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.610
Absolutely not!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:08.830
I'll make a list of what each one eats, 
so that all the attendants will know!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.340
I'll be back.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.080
Huh?

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.460
The sea sponge hasn't shrunk.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:23.440
What's wrong?

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.660
These ones aren't eating.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:29.790
Don't they eat what we found 
these sea slugs on?

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:31.880
They're supposed to.

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:34.330
All right.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.520
Let's try some other sea sponges.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:40.030
<b>The Great Sea Slug Debate</b>

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.030
The sea slugs aren't feeding?

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:48.270
Seven species are, 
but the Tambja sagamiana aren't.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.120
It's just one species. Figure it out.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.200
Give me a little more time.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.660
I want to gather some moss 
at a different shore.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.520
The exhibit starts at the end of the week.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:57.790
We aren't postponing it.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:58.940
But the food...

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.830
Let the attendant team figure it out.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.700
Get back to marketing work!

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.560
They aren't eating.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.620
This one's a no-go, too.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.560
Two more left...

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.030
What if they don't eat it, either?

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.030
There you are!

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:20.820
Kukuru!

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:23.340
The behind-the-scenes tour!

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:31.540
Penguins have a way of shooting their poop 
outside of their own nests.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.570
They can come at you really fast 
out of nowhere,

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:37.500
so we attendants get hit all the time.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.290
They shoot their poop?

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.110
Awesome!

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.870
Sorry I'm late!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.850
I'm Misakino, the guide.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:46.280
I'm really sorry!

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:49.630
I've introduced the tour already.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:51.070
Not to worry.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:52.830
Sorry.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.780
Would you move out of the way?

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:56.940
We're about to start feeding.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:58.110
Hi!

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:00.310
We've all been waiting 
for feeding time, haven't we?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.190
They start pecking at you 
if you don't go fast.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:08.070
So the trick is to be quick.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.790
Seriously.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.730
How could you forget the tour 
that you're in charge of?

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:18.550
This is why I can't stand Gama Gama.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.960
Is the other Gama Gama like that, too?

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:25.160
That one's a little more useful.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.010
How about yours?

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.260
Ours are...

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.620
They're a mixed bag.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:38.890
What's up?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.690
Sorry, this is urgent.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.940
Okay, later.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.160
Bye.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:49.780
Are you having lunch, Kaoru-chan?

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:52.070
Handmade bento, huh?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.790
Looks delicious.

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.910
Wow, what are you, a food guy?

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:57.500
Huh?

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.540
What?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.580
She's not a guy.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.660
Wait a second. Did you think Kaoru-chan's...

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.110
A woman?

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.300
Our Kuuya here's delicate.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.020
I need air!

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:27.770
Kukuru-san, we got an inquiry 
about the pamphlets.

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.870
Did we order the right number?

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:30.560
Huh?

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:31.200
Wait...

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:33.270
Shit!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:38.950
Kukuru, sorry, could you confirm
the merch once you're done there?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.860
Okay, got it.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.270
<i>What do I do about the sea slug exhibit?</i>

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:47.510
<i>I have to do something.</i>

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.480
Oh, Kai, it's you.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:02.720
For you.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.000
Thanks.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.420
Are you on late shift?

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.270
Yeah.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.990
I'm taking a short break.

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.120
Hey...

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:11.850
Yeah?

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.570
Is there anything I can do?

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:17.740
You have too much to do by yourself.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.880
If there's anything I can help with, 
let me know.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.660
Let me think...

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:23.460
There is!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:45.900
Sorry.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.630
No, I feel better.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:48.950
I'll go check on the sea slugs.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.380
Thanks, Kai!

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:55.430
I guess I should get to work, too.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.570
It's no good.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.080
It isn't shrinking.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:08.590
If they don't eat this one, 
I'll have to try sea moss.

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.020
And if that doesn't work...

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.620
Are they not eating?

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:20.540
We'll have to do the exhibit 
without feeding them.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.220
I won't do it without feeding!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:26.100
They aren't eating right now as it is.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:30.920
But we might stress them out even
more if we present them like this.

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:32.780
It'll be cruel to the sea slugs!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:33.990
Cruel?

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:37.580
What do you think aquariums exist for?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.870
We capture animals, trap them in tanks,

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.050
and have people look at them.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.750
That's what an aquarium is.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.750
If you care about the animals' happiness, 
aquariums shouldn't exist.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.310
Am I wrong?

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:54.110
That might be true,

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.180
but I want a lot of people
to see them and learn about them.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:58.340
That's contradictory.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.300
Then why do you think 
they exist, Shimabukuro-san?

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.100
To protect the planet.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:11.520
We study aquatic animals and present
and exhibit the results of our research.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:16.570
The main objective is to have people 
understand the wonders of life.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.780
I believe aquariums are the gateway to that.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:24.940
How do we coexist with the natural
world and all the creatures in it?

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:26.790
Isn't that what's most important?

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:31.540
What do you intend to do 
if we don't find food for this guy?

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:34.030
I'll take it back to the water.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.840
That's irresponsible.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:39.130
You brought it here, so it's your responsibility 
to take care of it until the end.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.220
But I can't watch it grow weaker!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:43.560
You were the one who brought
it here in the first place.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.890
That's why I'll take
responsibility and take it back.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:47.890
This isn't just about the sea slug.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.890
I want to save it first!

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.230
You're being narrow-minded.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.860
You're too broad-minded!

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.540
What is that supposed to mean?

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:03.870
Why sea slugs?

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.180
What's the reason?

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.370
I like them.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:09.360
And?

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.790
That's all.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.040
Sea slugs are full of mysteries.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:18.010
You wouldn't believe it, 
but they're a kind of water snail.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.600
There's a ton of species, 
and they're all different.

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:24.550
Some of them camouflage. 
Some of them have toxins.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:27.310
And they're just so colorful and pretty.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:31.310
I want more people to know 
how interesting sea slugs are.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.080
I get it.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.400
That's why you want to do the—

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.570
But I can't accept it!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.780
I won't accept not feeding them!

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.300
All right. I get what you're saying.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.660
But it isn't necessarily correct.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.700
There is no right or wrong answer 
to this problem.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:55.930
The most we can do is to think about 
what the best thing to do for the animals is,

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:59.210
and to be responsible for
the answers we come up with.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:01.920
I'll help you out, if you're okay with it.

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.180
I like thinking about animals.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.100
I do, too.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:09.370
We finally agree on something.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.110
Yeah.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.980
<b>Sea Slug Salad Bowl Exhibit</b>

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:21.900
They're so cute!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.240
They're gross.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.680
Let's buy some merch on our way out.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:25.610
Totally!

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:26.740
I hope they have hats!

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:32.250
What do you think, seeing them up close?

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.960
I thought it'd be worse.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.490
Actually, they're cuter than I imagined.

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.920
You should let Kukuru know.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.020
Thank goodness. There are a lot of people.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:45.390
Mom, there aren't any sea slugs.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.880
You're right.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:48.970
Maybe they're playing hide-and-seek.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:50.850
What is going on?!

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:55.320
We'll put the <i>Tambja sagamiana</i> in the exhibit, 
once we determine what they eat.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:57.310
Until then, we'll keep them in the back area.

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:00.020
Their condition will be the same
either way. So present them!

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:00.830
We can't.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:02.060
Move them immediately!

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:03.610
I said we can't!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.190
Plankton!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.290
Looks like he wrung you dry.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:19.240
Well, not everything went as we wanted, 
but I think we can call it a success.

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:21.300
Right!

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:24.190
By the way, do you have plans after?

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.300
No, I don't.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:28.260
I know of a good shore.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.520
I'll go!

00:23:02.100 --> 00:23:04.560
Sea slugs are very picky eaters.

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:08.240
They're difficult to raise, 
so they're not well-suited for exhibits.

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:12.240
And the reason we decided 
to show them off is

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:15.700
because one of the staff 
is passionate about them.

00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:21.870
This is courtship behavior.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:23.510
Huh?

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.300
Hey, get back to work.

00:23:25.970 --> 00:23:27.760
Are you listening, Kuuya-kun?

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:29.010
A'ight.

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.300
Nope. Nope. Nope. Nope.

00:23:32.310 --> 00:23:33.590
What's his deal?

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.220
Dunno.
